1
00:00:02,613 --> 00:00:05,517
“I was unfaithful to my wife.”

2
00:00:05,567 --> 00:00:10,357
That’s what Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang
tells his employees on November eighth.

3
00:00:10,407 --> 00:00:13,620
The same day, Nvidia opens
an independent investigation

4
00:00:13,670 --> 00:00:17,124
into whether a foreign
intelligence service targeted him.

5
00:00:17,174 --> 00:00:20,263
The woman at the center
of the allegation is Alice Huang.

6
00:00:20,313 --> 00:00:23,029
She comes from the other side
of Nvidia’s business.

7
00:00:23,079 --> 00:00:26,043
The company she helps build
buys the kinds of chips

8
00:00:26,093 --> 00:00:29,010
Washington is trying
to keep out of China.

9
00:00:39,686 --> 00:00:45,482
In October 2022, the United States
announces a new set of export controls.

10
00:00:45,532 --> 00:00:49,586
Shipments of certain advanced
processors to China are restricted.

11
00:00:49,636 --> 00:00:53,802
Washington says the same computing power
that drives commercial research

12
00:00:53,852 --> 00:00:57,629
can also help China build more
advanced military systems.

13
00:00:57,679 --> 00:01:01,762
One of the chips caught up
in those restrictions is Nvidia’s H100.

14
00:01:01,812 --> 00:01:04,063
Put enough of them together
in a data center

15
00:01:04,113 --> 00:01:06,435
and they can split the work
of training an AI model

16
00:01:06,485 --> 00:01:08,715
across a whole bank of machines.

17
00:01:08,765 --> 00:01:11,206
For a company trying to get
that computing power,

18
00:01:11,256 --> 00:01:12,966
there are two ways to go about it.

19
00:01:13,016 --> 00:01:15,674
You can buy the hardware
and install it yourself.

20
00:01:15,724 --> 00:01:18,287
Or you can pay to use someone else’s.

21
00:01:18,337 --> 00:01:21,645
The machines can be in one country
and the person sending them work

22
00:01:21,695 --> 00:01:22,771
can be in another.

23
00:01:22,821 --> 00:01:26,049
The data moves.
The chips stay in the rack.

24
00:01:26,099 --> 00:01:29,395
That distinction matters because
a shipping record can tell you

25
00:01:29,445 --> 00:01:31,203
where a machine was delivered.

26
00:01:31,253 --> 00:01:33,976
A different set of records
would tell you who rented it

27
00:01:34,026 --> 00:01:35,593
and where they connected from.

28
00:01:35,643 --> 00:01:38,105
That’s the business
Alice Huang moves into.

29
00:01:38,155 --> 00:01:40,598
She comes from Shanghai’s
investment world.

30
00:01:40,648 --> 00:01:45,080
In 2023, she takes control
of a Singapore company called Megaspeed.

31
00:01:45,130 --> 00:01:48,041
It began as a subsidiary
of a video game developer.

32
00:01:48,091 --> 00:01:50,675
It becomes an Nvidia cloud partner.

33
00:01:50,725 --> 00:01:52,464
By the end of 2023,

34
00:01:52,514 --> 00:01:56,654
a Singapore company called SwiftData
has taken ownership of Megaspeed.

35
00:01:56,704 --> 00:01:58,286
Look at Megaspeed’s filings.

36
00:01:58,336 --> 00:02:02,971
In 2023, the company reports
thirty-three million dollars in assets.

37
00:02:03,021 --> 00:02:05,652
A year later, it reports three billion.

38
00:02:05,702 --> 00:02:08,755
And when Alice and a business partner
pitch a new data center project

39
00:02:08,805 --> 00:02:12,915
to investors in early 2025,
an investor tells the Financial Times

40
00:02:12,965 --> 00:02:17,168
that the pair makes a point of how
easily they can get Nvidia GPUs.

41
00:02:17,218 --> 00:02:20,839
The investor says they name Alibaba
as a client for the project.

42
00:02:20,889 --> 00:02:23,352
The chip deliveries leave their own trail.

43
00:02:23,402 --> 00:02:27,498
Shipping records reviewed by Reuters
show Megaspeed’s Indonesian subsidiary

44
00:02:27,548 --> 00:02:31,478
importing Nvidia hardware
between 2024 and 2026.

45
00:02:31,528 --> 00:02:33,792
The records include H100s.

46
00:02:33,842 --> 00:02:37,320
Those shipments establish
that the hardware reached Indonesia.

47
00:02:37,370 --> 00:02:40,704
The next question is
who could use it, and from where.

48
00:02:40,754 --> 00:02:43,995
By October 2025,
the New York Times reports

49
00:02:44,045 --> 00:02:47,584
that U.S. authorities are looking
into whether Megaspeed helped

50
00:02:47,634 --> 00:02:53,097
Chinese companies get access to advanced
chips covered by American export controls.

51
00:02:53,147 --> 00:02:55,735
Singapore police confirm
their own investigation

52
00:02:55,785 --> 00:02:58,512
into possible breaches of Singapore law.

53
00:02:58,562 --> 00:03:02,151
Megaspeed denies illicit
activity involving chips.

54
00:03:02,201 --> 00:03:06,315
On October tenth, reporters from
the Straits Times visit Megaspeed’s office

55
00:03:06,365 --> 00:03:09,917
on the seventh floor
of Singapore’s Ocean Financial Centre.

56
00:03:09,967 --> 00:03:14,397
The glass door is locked. They can see
two gray armchairs in reception.

57
00:03:14,447 --> 00:03:16,565
The company’s nameplate is still there.

58
00:03:20,057 --> 00:03:23,091
At the 2024 Computex trade show in Taiwan,

59
00:03:23,141 --> 00:03:26,641
a server manufacturer called
Gigabyte throws a party.

60
00:03:26,691 --> 00:03:28,757
Its servers use Nvidia chips.

61
00:03:28,807 --> 00:03:33,012
A person who attends tells Reuters
that both Alice and Jensen are there.

62
00:03:33,062 --> 00:03:36,635
In a photo posted on LinkedIn,
the two are sitting side by side.

63
00:03:36,685 --> 00:03:40,387
Then there’s video.
On May twenty-second, 2025,

64
00:03:40,437 --> 00:03:44,489
Taiwanese television footage shows
a group dinner at a restaurant in Taipei.

65
00:03:44,539 --> 00:03:46,078
Reuters later compares the footage

66
00:03:46,128 --> 00:03:49,505
with a separate photograph
and identifies Alice at the table.

67
00:03:49,555 --> 00:03:51,075
Jensen is there too.

68
00:03:51,125 --> 00:03:53,692
Their companies have a clear
business connection.

69
00:03:53,742 --> 00:03:58,712
The espionage allegation traces back
to a document circulating in Washington.

70
00:03:58,762 --> 00:04:01,944
In the spring of 2026,
according to the New York Times,

71
00:04:01,994 --> 00:04:05,776
a memo circulates among senior officials
in the Trump administration.

72
00:04:05,826 --> 00:04:08,838
People briefed on the intelligence
tell the paper that China’s

73
00:04:08,888 --> 00:04:11,358
Ministry of State Security
recruited Alice Huang

74
00:04:11,408 --> 00:04:13,575
to gather information on Jensen.

75
00:04:13,625 --> 00:04:17,458
The reported goal includes learning more
about America’s advanced AI chips

76
00:04:17,508 --> 00:04:21,607
and potentially getting Nvidia
to push for broader sales to China.

77
00:04:21,657 --> 00:04:24,752
The allegation puts a different
kind of information at stake.

78
00:04:24,802 --> 00:04:27,476
A chip is something you can trace
through a shipment.

79
00:04:27,526 --> 00:04:29,718
A company’s plans
for what it wants to sell,

80
00:04:29,768 --> 00:04:34,095
or what it’s asking Washington to approve,
can travel in a conversation.

81
00:04:34,145 --> 00:04:37,303
Consider how much a single decision
in Washington can change.

82
00:04:37,353 --> 00:04:41,578
In April 2025, the U.S. government
tells Nvidia it needs a license

83
00:04:41,628 --> 00:04:44,811
to sell a different chip,
the H20, into China.

84
00:04:44,861 --> 00:04:48,173
Nvidia later reports
a four and a half billion dollar charge

85
00:04:48,223 --> 00:04:51,291
tied to inventory and purchase
commitments for that chip.

86
00:04:51,341 --> 00:04:54,913
Knowing which processors Washington
might clear for sale, and when,

87
00:04:54,963 --> 00:04:57,548
could shape where a customer
spends billions.

88
00:04:57,598 --> 00:05:01,588
On October twenty-ninth, the Times
makes the suspected operation public.

89
00:05:02,328 --> 00:05:05,378
Nvidia says its CEO routinely
meets with customers

90
00:05:05,428 --> 00:05:09,375
and that its regional cloud customers
receive ordinary business information.

91
00:05:09,425 --> 00:05:12,770
China’s Foreign Ministry later
rejects the spying allegation.

92
00:05:12,820 --> 00:05:15,718
Reuters says it was unable
to verify it independently,

93
00:05:15,768 --> 00:05:18,458
and reporters at both Reuters
and the Financial Times

94
00:05:18,508 --> 00:05:20,708
were unable to reach Alice for comment.

95
00:05:24,328 --> 00:05:28,455
In Washington, three House committee
chairs send Jensen a letter.

96
00:05:28,505 --> 00:05:30,668
They want him to brief them
behind closed doors

97
00:05:30,718 --> 00:05:34,848
about his contacts with Alice Huang
and what Nvidia does to protect itself

98
00:05:34,898 --> 00:05:36,534
from foreign espionage.

99
00:05:36,584 --> 00:05:38,928
They request November eighteenth.

100
00:05:38,978 --> 00:05:40,850
Four days after the letter is dated,

101
00:05:40,900 --> 00:05:43,799
Jensen sends the email
admitting to an affair.

102
00:05:43,849 --> 00:05:46,992
He says he’ll cooperate fully
with the board’s investigation.

103
00:05:47,042 --> 00:05:49,647
His message leaves
the other person unnamed.

104
00:05:49,697 --> 00:05:53,772
The Times and the Financial Times
identify her as Alice Huang.

105
00:05:53,822 --> 00:05:56,468
When Nvidia’s board
announces its investigation,

106
00:05:56,518 --> 00:05:59,128
it says it has no reason
to believe company secrets

107
00:05:59,178 --> 00:06:01,604
or national security were compromised.

108
00:06:01,654 --> 00:06:05,765
The next day, President Trump says
the FBI is looking into the matter.

109
00:06:05,815 --> 00:06:10,203
On November tenth, Nvidia names the lawyer
who will lead the outside investigation.

110
00:06:10,253 --> 00:06:14,223
Joon H. Kim is a former acting
U.S. attorney in Manhattan.

111
00:06:14,273 --> 00:06:16,849
A shareholder lawsuit
adds another question.

112
00:06:16,899 --> 00:06:20,828
The complaint accuses Nvidia
and its CEO of misleading investors

113
00:06:20,878 --> 00:06:24,324
about the risks surrounding
the company’s dealings with Megaspeed.

114
00:06:24,374 --> 00:06:26,766
Those allegations are now before a court.

115
00:06:26,816 --> 00:06:28,308
As of November eleventh,

116
00:06:28,358 --> 00:06:31,918
there’s been no public finding
that Megaspeed broke export rules.

117
00:06:31,968 --> 00:06:34,794
Nvidia’s board has yet
to publish its conclusions.

118
00:06:34,844 --> 00:06:37,588
And the evidence behind the reported
intelligence assessment

119
00:06:37,638 --> 00:06:39,538
is still out of public view.

120
00:06:40,191 --> 00:06:42,768
If Jensen gives Congress
the briefing it requested,

121
00:06:42,818 --> 00:06:45,122
it will take place behind closed doors.

122
00:06:45,172 --> 00:06:47,028
The question on the other side
of those doors

123
00:06:47,078 --> 00:06:49,812
is the one the public still can’t answer.

124
00:06:49,862 --> 00:06:52,878
What, if anything, reached Beijing?

